{
  "dom_id": "step-q96946",
  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "The table below gives the values of ${\u03a6}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=\u03a6(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z>z)=0.45.$\n\n| $\\,p\\,$ | $0.55$ | $0.60$ | $0.65$ | $0.70$ | $0.75$ | $0.80$ | $0.85$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${\u03a6}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,0.1257\\,$ | $\\,0.2533\\,$ | $\\,0.3853\\,$ | $\\,0.5244\\,$ | $\\,0.6745\\,$ | $\\,0.8416\\,$ | $\\,1.0364\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "First, we express the given information in terms of $\u03a6,$ using the complement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z>z) & =0.45 \\\\ 1-P(Z\\le z) & =0.45 \\\\ 1-\u03a6(z) & =0.45 \\\\ \u03a6(z) & =1-0.45 \\\\ \u03a6(z) & =0.55\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={\u03a6}^{-1}(0.55).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.55,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.55\\,\u21d2\\,{\u03a6}^{-1}(p)=0.1257.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={\u03a6}^{-1}(0.55)=0.1257.\n$$",
